From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:00:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Report language servers that fail to start or
 initialize, or that stop

Helix logged these cases only, so a wrong server path or a server that
crashed left a document without diagnostics and no word why.

- A server that cannot be started shows "Language server NAME did not
  start: ..." in the status line. A missing command is still silent when
  it is a bare name (servers that are simply not installed), and reported
  when it was configured by its path. "Loaded N files" at start-up no
  longer replaces such an error.
- A failed initialize request is reported with the server's name.
- A server that ends while Helix still uses it reports that it stopped
  unexpectedly (or ended before it was ready); a server stopped by Helix
  keeps the old "Language server exited".

One message per event; a document open retries the start once.
